The carmar package is released under the MIT license; the two-line LICENSE
file names the year and the copyright holder, and the full text is R's
MIT license template (https://www.r-project.org/Licenses/MIT).

Bundled components
------------------

The package carries, under inst/, files that are not R code:

  inst/app/kernel/*.R, index.html      MIT   Mohammed Saqr
  inst/app/carmar_V<version>.html      MIT   Mohammed Saqr (built from the
                                             CarmaR sources and @carmnote/core
                                             0.5.0, both MIT, same author)
  inst/app/kernel/mcp/carmar-mcp.mjs   MIT   Mohammed Saqr
  inst/app/lib/*.js                    MIT   Mohammed Saqr
  inst/quarto/_extensions/carmar/*     MIT   Mohammed Saqr

The notebook page also carries editor colour palettes whose colour values
come from the Ace editor's themes (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2010, Ajax.org
B.V.), as data, not code — see inst/AUTHORS.

No third-party library is bundled. See inst/AUTHORS for the verification and
for the resources the notebook page may fetch at runtime, which are not part
of this package.
